<sn><md>### Example

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
**local** {.text-center}
```bash
emon@emon:~$ rclone lsf Documents/
Books/
bcs learning setup for linux.md
note.txt
note2.md
syllabus.md
```
:::

:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
**Remote** {.text-center}
```bash
emon@emon:~$ rclone lsf gd:BCS
BCS 10-50 QNA.zip
Bangla Grammer/
Bangla Literature/
Bangladesh  Affairs/
Computer and ICT/
English Grammar/
English Literature/
General Science/
Geography/
International Affairs/
QNA/
math/

```
:::
:::

</md></sn><sn><md>### Apply `-R` flag

```
Books/ &lt;--- Folder
bcs learning setup for linux.md
note.txt
note2.md
syllabus.md
Books/Chemistry.pdf
Books/Math.pdf
Books/Notes/ &lt;---- Folder
Books/Physics.pdf
Books/Notes/chemistry_note.md
Books/Notes/math_note.md
Books/Notes/physics_note.md
```
</md></sn><sn><md>### Apply Flags

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
**list files only** {.text-center}

Use:

```bash
rclone lsf --files-only gdrive:
```

Output:

```text
notes.txt
image.jpg
Backup/data.zip
```
:::

:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
**list folder only** {.text-center}

Use:

```bash
rclone lsf --dirs-only gdrive:
```

Output:

```text
Documents/
Photos/
Backup/
```
:::
:::

**Show File Sizes**

Use the `-s` / `--size` option:

```bash
rclone lsf --size gdrive:
```

Example:

```text
2048 notes.txt
1048576 image.jpg
```

**Show Modification Time**

Use:

```bash
rclone lsf --modtime gdrive:
```

Example:

```text
2026-09-01 08:30:15 notes.txt
2026-08-30 14:20:10 image.jpg
```

</md></sn><sn><md>### Useful `lsf` Options

| Command                             | Result                     |
| ----------------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| `rclone lsf gdrive:`                | Files and directories      |
| `rclone lsf --files-only gdrive:`   | Files only                 |
| `rclone lsf --dirs-only gdrive:`    | Directories only           |
| `rclone lsf --size gdrive:`         | Include file sizes         |
| `rclone lsf --modtime gdrive:`      | Include modification times |
| `rclone lsf --recursive gdrive:`    | Search recursively         |
| `rclone lsf --format "pst" gdrive:` | Custom output format       |
</md></sn><sn><md>#### Why Use `lsf`?

`lsf` is particularly useful for **scripts and automation** because its output is simple and can be customized.

For example:

```bash
rclone lsf --files-only --recursive gdrive:Documents
```

could produce:

```text
notes.txt
Physics/chapter1.pdf
Physics/chapter2.pdf
Programming/C/lesson1.c
Programming/C/lesson2.c
```

This makes it easier to pass Rclone's output to other Linux commands or scripts.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Summary

**rclone lsf** {.text-center}

- Displays a precise list of files and folders within a directory.
- Print file/Dir name only
- By default not recursive,but can be with `-R` flag
- Useful flags include `--files-only`,`--dirs-only`,`--size`,`modtime`
</md></sn>